From: Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:16:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: seal a database's pages in application-services, for
 encriox

sql-support gains obfsvfs, for an app that keeps its databases sealed:
encriox's spike, whose history, bookmarks, logins and cards are sealed
with keys from the user's vault (encri-firefox, stage 3). It is the
scheme of Gecko's obfuscating VFS, brought to application-services'
own SQLite with AES-256-GCM from NSS: each 8192-byte page, its log's
and its journal's, sealed under a key given in the database's URI.

A page that does not open under its key is an I/O error, never a
corrupt database, which places and autofill delete and make again. On
Android, where application-services has a SQLite of its own, it is
SQLite's default VFS before any database opens, and refuses a sealed
database opened without its key, and one in the clear with a key.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
